# tool: Themes

The colour presets the interface can wear.

A theme is four colours and a dial — a surface, an ink, an accent, and how
strongly the layers between them separate. Everything else is derived: the
cards, the borders, the chart series, and the colour of every memory category
in the graph.

## Commands
- **list** — the themes available, built-in first
- **get** — one theme with the CSS properties it renders to
- **install** — add a preset of your own
- **delete** — remove one of yours

## When to use
- **Someone asks to change how the app looks:** list, then set it in config
- **Someone brings a palette:** install it as a preset

## When NOT to use
- Not to change one colour in one screen — that is a component, not a theme

Composite tool `Themes` with 4 actions: delete, get, install, list.

Every colour the interface uses comes from a token, and every token is derived
from the four colours a theme declares. That is why a theme is short, and why a
palette that renders an unreadable interface is caught when it is installed
rather than when somebody squints at it.

A theme with both a light and a dark palette can follow the system. One with a
single palette cannot honour a preference it has no colours for.

## Usage
Call as `Themes({ action: "<action>", input: { ... }, _reasoning: "..." })`.
Set `schema: true` on the same level as `action` to receive the full action detail (description, examples, input schema, token estimate) instead of executing.

## actions

### themes_delete

Remove a theme you installed.

Delete one of your presets.

A built-in theme cannot be removed: it lives in the binary, so deleting it would
only mean pretending it is not there.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Identifier of the theme."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### themes_get

Read one theme and what it renders to.

One theme: the palette its author wrote, and the CSS custom properties
that palette produces for each appearance it offers.

The rendered properties are what the interface actually sets on the document
root. Reading them is how you find out what a theme will look like without
switching to it.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Identifier of the theme."
    },
    "appearance": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Which palette to render. Defaults to both."
    },
    "native": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "True when rendering for the desktop window, where a translucent background has something behind it."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### themes_install

Add a theme of your own.

Install a preset.

It is rendered and checked before it is stored: a palette that produces fewer
properties than the interface reads is refused here rather than discovered later
as an element nobody can see.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Identifier for the theme. Example: \"my-theme\"."
    },
    "name": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Human-readable name. Defaults to the identifier."
    },
    "author": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Who made it."
    },
    "variants": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Palettes by appearance. A theme with both light and dark can follow the system.",
      "additionalProperties": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "surface": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Background colour of the application, as a hex value."
          },
          "ink": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Colour of text on the surface, as a hex value."
          },
          "accent": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Primary accent, as a hex value."
          },
          "contrast": {
            "type": "integer",
            "description": "How strongly derived layers separate from the surface, 0 to 100. 50 is neutral."
          },
          "radius": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Corner rounding: none, sm, md or lg."
          },
          "windows": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "solid or blur. Blur asks the operating system for a translucent window."
          },
          "semantic": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Colours by meaning: accent, success, warning, error, info, diffAdded, diffRemoved.",
            "additionalProperties": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "surface",
          "ink",
          "accent",
          "contrast"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "variants",
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

### themes_list

List the themes available.

The presets this build ships with, followed by the ones installed here.

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "appearance": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only themes that offer this appearance: light, dark or auto."
    },
    "_reasoning": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MANDATORY. NEVER FORGET. Explain why this specific tool is being called now, what outcome you expect, and the immediate next step if that helps clarify the call. Do not leave this empty.",
      "minLength": 1
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "_reasoning"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

